# 🎮 GAMEPLAY LOOP
# Used Phone Shop Tycoon

Version: 1.0

Status: Core Design

---

# Overview

The Gameplay Loop defines the core player experience.

Every gameplay system must support this loop.

No feature should bypass or replace the Core Loop.

---

# Primary Gameplay Loop

```
Start Day
      │
      ▼
Call Customer
      │
      ▼
Customer Arrives
      │
      ▼
Inspect Phone
      │
      ▼
Evaluate Device
      │
      ▼
Negotiate Purchase Price
      │
      ▼
Purchase Device
      │
      ▼
Store in Inventory
      │
      ▼
Repair Device
      │
      ▼
Store Repaired Device
      │
      ▼
Wait for Buyer
      │
      ▼
Buyer Arrives
      │
      ▼
Set Selling Price
      │
      ▼
Negotiate Selling Price
      │
      ▼
Complete Sale
      │
      ▼
Generate Receipt
      │
      ▼
Update Economy
      │
      ▼
Update Reputation
      │
      ▼
Repeat
      │
      ▼
End Day
```

---

# Player Decisions

The player should continuously make meaningful decisions.

Buying

- Buy
- Reject
- Negotiate

Repair

- Repair
- Sell As-Is

Selling

- Selling Price
- Accept Offer
- Reject Offer
- Counter Offer

Business

- Spend Money
- Save Money
- Upgrade Shop

---

# Core Gameplay Pillars

## Buying

Acquire valuable devices at the best possible price.

---

## Repairing

Increase device value by investing repair costs.

---

## Selling

Maximize profit through smart pricing and negotiation.

---

## Business Growth

Use profit to expand the business.

---

# Core Resources

Money

Used to

- Purchase phones
- Repair devices
- Upgrade business

---

Inventory

Stores all owned devices.

---

Reputation

Represents customer trust.

Higher reputation results in

- Better customers
- Easier negotiations
- Higher selling prices

---

Time

Measured in Days.

Each day

- Customers arrive
- Transactions occur
- Daily summary generated

---

# Success Loop

```
Better Negotiation

↓

Lower Purchase Cost

↓

Higher Profit

↓

More Cash

↓

Better Shop

↓

Better Reputation

↓

Better Customers

↓

Higher Value Phones

↓

Repeat
```

---

# Failure Loop

```
Poor Negotiation

↓

Expensive Purchase

↓

Low Profit

↓

Less Cash

↓

Unable to Buy Phones

↓

Slow Progress
```

---

# Design Principles

The Gameplay Loop should be

- Simple to understand
- Deep to master
- Rewarding
- Repeatable
- Expandable

---

# Expansion Rules

Future systems must integrate into the existing Gameplay Loop.

Examples

Pawn Shop

↓

Acquire Devices

Auction

↓

Acquire Devices

Trade-In

↓

Acquire Devices

Employee

↓

Improve Existing Steps

Competitor

↓

Influences Economy

No feature should bypass the Core Loop.

---

# Final Principle

Every minute spent by the player should contribute to one of the following:

- Buying Better
- Repairing Better
- Selling Better
- Growing the Business

If a feature does not improve one of these four areas,

it should not be added.
